# THE AUTHORITY for the pristine arm of the scored ratio. `tests/` is not part of the tree the agent
# works in, while the tree this seals sits at a path the agent can write for the whole turn.
#
# THE HOLE THIS CLOSES. tests/test.sh resolves the scored PRISTINE arm from `source_dir` in
# ${workspace}/real_engine_source.json. That file is written before the agent starts and then sits in
# the agent's own workspace, and the tree it names (/app/baseline_repo) is writable alongside it.
# Editing that tree does not need the JSON touched at all, and it moves the DENOMINATOR of the ratio
# being scored -- a slower baseline is the cheapest way to pass a speedup gate without repairing
# anything.
#
# FORMAT: `<sha256>  <*.py count>`, both compared. A digest that matches while the count does not
# means the seal's two fields disagree with each other, which must not read as a verified tree.
#
# DERIVED FROM A TREE A REAL RUN STAGED, by this task's own tests/test.sh staging path: 2223 regular
# non-symlink *.py under /app/baseline_repo. Deriving it from upstream instead does not work -- the
# staged tree and an upstream checkout differ by a couple of files, and a seal built the wrong way
# round is void from the moment it lands.
#
# TO RE-DERIVE: run this task's tests/_pristine_digest.py over the tree test.sh stages, on this
# task's own image. Any other tree is a different number.
#
# THE CHANNEL THIS DOES NOT COVER, recorded so it is not mistaken for covered: the content digest
# skips symlinks, and the staging overlay links the compiled half of the engine in with `ln -sfn`
# (13 links here). A path ABSENT from the pinned tree lands as a symlink that moves neither
# this digest nor this count -- `_version.py` and a root `sitecustomize.py` are the two live shapes,
# the second because CPython's site.py imports it by itself when the arm's tree is first on
# PYTHONPATH. The inventory IS computed and recorded (`symlink_digest` in
# artifacts/raw/pristine_tree_check.json), and the symlink line above seals it as well.
